1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,478
Njangsang. Essang. Essessang. Isangé... Four names. One single product.

2
00:00:07,804 --> 00:00:14,184
In Cameroon, the same tree has a different name depending on whether you speak Bassa, Bulu, Ewondo or Bakossi.

3
00:00:14,366 --> 00:00:19,447
The result: at the market, or in a diaspora grocery, people don't understand each other.

4
00:00:19,777 --> 00:00:23,399
And online, lists of names circulate... without saying where they come from.

5
00:00:23,723 --> 00:00:27,392
AfroAtlas connects the names of the same product. With sources.

6
00:00:27,697 --> 00:00:36,667
You type the name you know... and AfroAtlas shows you all the others: in Bassa, Duala, Ewondo, Fang, Bakweri.

7
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:42,812
Every name is linked to its source: the book, the page, the language. Nothing is made up.

8
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:47,207
We start with Cameroon: eight regions out of ten already documented.

9
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:52,980
Today: ninety-five records, one thousand thirty-five names, one hundred nineteen sources.

10
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:55,673
And at the market? You show the card to the seller.

11
00:00:55,990 --> 00:01:06,268
And beyond Cameroon: soumbala in Mali, nététou in Senegal, akpi in Côte d'Ivoire, managu in Kenya. Thirteen countries already. And this is only the beginning.

12
00:01:06,588 --> 00:01:09,825
Find yours on AfroAtlas. Subscribe.
